pl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORISHI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO TETSUJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SONY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORISHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, TETSUJIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SONY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORISHI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO TETSUJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORISHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, TETSUJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Conventionally, it is necessary to allocate a certain amount of information to an edge portion so as to code a digital image signal, and hence there is a limitation of reduction of the amount of information, degrading the coding efficiency. A coding device divides an image signal including information on pixels of, e.g. frame unit into macroblocks, groups items of information on pixels correlated with each other in each macroblock, and codes pixel information in each group based on level data representing the signal level of the item of information on a representative pixel in each group, position data of all the pixel information in each group, and number-of-pixels data representing the number of items of the pixel information in each group.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Traditionnellement, il est nécessaire d'attribuer une certaine quantité d'informations à une partie bordure de façon à coder un signal d'image numérique. Il en résulte donc une limitation de la réduction de la quantité d'informations, ce qui affaiblit l'efficacité de codage. Un dispositif de codage divise un signal d'image comportant des informations sur des pixels, par ex. une unité de trame, en macroblocs, groupe les éléments d'information sur les pixels corrélés les uns avec les autres dans chaque macrobloc et code les informations de pixels dans chaque groupe sur la base de données de niveaux représentant le niveau de signal de l'élément d'information sur un pixel représentatif de chaque groupe, les données de position de toutes les informations de pixels dans chaque groupe et les données de nombre de pixels représentant le nombre d'éléments des informations de pixel dans chaque groupe.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>